    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know you're trying to be positive but you don't get it. it's not about 'working on things' anymore. when something is broken beyond repair, you don't keep trying to fix it and making a mess, you just remove it so it stops causing damage. they deserve to breathe, to be happy, to not have to worry about me every single second. if i'm gone, the constant weight is gone. isn't that just a kinder way to look at it?",
